# Class: obo:HMDM_0000032 (cardiac glycoside reductase (cgr) operon)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:23869020") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HMDM_0000032 "A specific bacterial enzyme that allows E. lenta bacteria to metabolize and deactivate digoxin.")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:HMDM_0000032 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace obo:HMDM_0000032 "human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:HMDM_0000032 "HMDM:0000032")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HMDM_0000032 "cardiac glycoside reductase (cgr) operon")
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000032 obo:HMDM_0000095)

# Class: obo:HMDM_0000035 (Eggerthella lenta cgr1)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:21304654") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:23869020") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HMDM_0000035 "This gene is responsible for encoding proteins which are homologous to bacterial cytochromes, this allows the bacteria to use digoxin as an alternate electron acceptor.  Cgr1 is not directly involved in digoxin reduction, instead, it has a more general function such as electron transfer, or membrane docking. The function of cgr1 is thought to be completing the electron transfer from a membrane-associated electron donor (e.g. the membrane quinone pool) to the [4Fe-4S] cluster of the Cgr2 reductase via its covalently bound heme groups. It is highly up-regulated by digoxin and other cardiac glycosides containing unsaturated butyrolactone rings, such as digitoxin, digoxigenin, and, to a lesser extent, ouabain. It is repressed by arginine but not by ornithine. It is a part of an operon that consists of cgr1 and cgr2.")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:HMDM_0000035 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace obo:HMDM_0000035 "human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:HMDM_0000035 "HMDM:0000035")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HMDM_0000035 "Eggerthella lenta cgr1")
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000035 obo:HMDM_0000095)
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000035 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:MOP_0000615 obo:HMDM_0000037))
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000035 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000050 obo:HMDM_0000032))

# Class: obo:HMDM_0000037 (Eggerthella lenta cgr2)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:21304654") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:23869020") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:29761785") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HMDM_0000037 "This gene is involved in the inactivation of the cardiac medication and plant natural product digoxin, thus decreasing drug efficacy and toxicity. It catalyzes the reduction of the alpha,beta-unsaturated butyrolactone ring of digoxin to the inactive metabolite dihydrodigoxin. It likely uses the cytochrome Cgr1 as the physiological electron donor, encoded by the adjacent gene in the locus. cgr2 only reduces digoxin and other cardenolide toxins, such as digitoxin, digoxigenin, ouabain and ouabagenin. Therefore, it is a specialized enzyme present in some gut bacteria E. lenta that protects their human host against ingested plant toxins.")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:HMDM_0000037 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace obo:HMDM_0000037 "human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:HMDM_0000037 "HMDM:0000037")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HMDM_0000037 "Eggerthella lenta cgr2")
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000037 obo:HMDM_0000095)
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000037 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:MOP_0000569 obo:CHEBI_28544))
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000037 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:MOP_0000569 obo:CHEBI_42098))
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000037 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:MOP_0000569 obo:CHEBI_4551))
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000037 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000050 obo:HMDM_0000032))
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000037 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000056 obo:HMDM_0000142))

# Class: obo:HMDM_0000049 (Beta-glucuronidase)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:28578872") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HMDM_0000049 "Beta-glucuronidases are members of the glycosidase family of enzymes that catalyze breakdown of complex carbohydrates. Bacterial beta-glucuronidase can metabolize to 18-beta-glycyrrhetinic acid (GA) as a main product and to 18-beta-glycyrrhetinic acid-3-O-beta-D-glucuronide (GAMG) as a minor product.")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:HMDM_0000049 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace obo:HMDM_0000049 "human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:HMDM_0000049 "HMDM:0000049")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HMDM_0000049 "Beta-glucuronidase")
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000049 obo:HMDM_0000493)

# Class: obo:HMDM_0000050 (Escherichia coli  uridine phosphorylase (udp))

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:32526207") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:34260950") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HMDM_0000050 "The uridine phosphorylase catalyzes the reversible conversion of uridine to uracil and ribose-1-phosphate in bacteria. This enzyme efficiently deglycosylates capecitabine, deoxyuridine, and doxifluridine.")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:HMDM_0000050 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280>)
