# Class: obo:HMDM_0000820 (pfkB family carbohydrate kinase)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:28441933") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HMDM_0000820 "The pfkB family of enzymes across kingdoms includes ribokinases, phosphofructokinases, adenosine kinases (ADKs) and several others with diverse substrate specificities. Typical PfkB protein structure is a large domain consisting of a beta-sheet sandwiched between several alpha-helices, and a smaller domain, known as the lid domain, comprised of another beta-sheet attached to the larger domain by short loops that act as a hinge. Binding of substrates to pfkB proteins follows ordered bi-bi kinetics where the carbohydrate enters first, followed by ATP. PfkB proteins possess two signature motifs: a di-gly (GG) motif in the N-terminal region and a G/AXGD motif in the C-terminal region. The role of each motif has been identified through mutational and structural analyses. The GG motif provides flexibility in the hinge region that connects the lid and the large domain. The aspartate in the G/AXGD motif acts as a base during catalysis and activates the C6 fructose hydroxyl group for nucleophilic attack on the gamma-phosphate in ATP. Many pfkB proteins are active as dimers generated through interactions between the lid domains of two monomers. Aside from their regulation by ATP, pfkB family enzymes are activated by both monovalent and divalent cationic cofactors.")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:HMDM_0000820 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace obo:HMDM_0000820 "human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:HMDM_0000820 "HMDM:0000820")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HMDM_0000820 "pfkB family carbohydrate kinase")
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000820 obo:HMDM_0000012)
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000820 obo:HMDM_0000901)

