# Class: obo:HMDM_0000830 (Glycoside hydrolase family 13)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:17085431") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:26090361") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HMDM_0000830 "Glycoside hydrolases (GHs) (EC 3.2.1.X) hydrolyze glycosidic bonds between carbohydrates or between carbohydrate and non-carbohydrate components, for instance alcohols or phenols. To date, enzyme classification is based on amino acid similarities rather than substrate specificity. GHs are assigned to different groups based on conserved domains, and the families are numbered from 1 to 131 that are listed in the Carbohydrate-Active Enzymes Database. Family GH13, also known as the alpha-amylase family, is the largest sequence-based family of glycoside hydrolases and groups together a number of different enzyme activities and substrate specificities acting on alpha-glycosidic bonds.")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:HMDM_0000830 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace obo:HMDM_0000830 "human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id obo:HMDM_0000830 "HMDM:0000830")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:HMDM_0000830 "Glycoside hydrolase family 13")
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000830 obo:HMDM_0000012)
SubClassOf(obo:HMDM_0000830 obo:HMDM_0000896)

