# Class: obo:HMDM_0000933 (Pseudomonas aeruginosa CYP107S1)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:39032655") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:HMDM_0000933 "CYP107S1 is a cytochrome P450 (CYP) enzyme found in the bacterium Pseudomonas aeruginosa. It can metabolize fluoroquinolone antibiotics (ciprofloxacin and fleroxacin), a cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator potentiator (ivacaftor), and a selective estrogen receptor modulator antimicrobial adjuvant (raloxifene).")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:contributor obo:HMDM_0000933 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9259-5280>)
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace obo:HMDM_0000933 "human_microbiome_drug_metabolism_ontology")
